ility for the first time  foreign  the biggest channel that called out Thai  was h3h3 Productions he was able to find  Thai's house on Zillow now technically  the listing does say off-market but  Ethan from H3 would describe Zillow as a  short-term rental website and it  basically alleged that Tai was just  renting this house for his videos and  given that this video got over 6 million  views and it led to quite a bit of drama  more people would start looking at the  time and the more they looked the more  they realized that Tai basically had no  background or reputation other than the  one that he portrayed on his YouTube  channel for obvious reasons this made  people quite suspicious Tai would go on  to address this video head-on by  inviting Ethan to his quote-unquote  rented house Tai would give Ethan a tour  of the house and show him his supercars  and whatnot Tai was probably hoping that  this confrontation would give him more  credibility and it to his credit he did  explain himself pretty well he came  clean about how he didn't own many of  the things he showed off like his house  and cars and that he leased them instead  he also clarified that he leased these  items not because he couldn't afford  demo but because it made more financial  sense to lease and there is a truth to  this it makes no sense to sink a quarter  million into a Lamborghini or 15 million  into a mansion when you can invest this  money into things like Google Apple  Tesla the S P 500 or your own business  which would all likely generate far  higher returns so while Ty did have an  explanation as to why he released people  didn't exactly trust them and it wasn't  because his explanation was bad or that  people suspected that he wasn't actually  rich honestly his wealth never really  should have been the question from the  start to run the type of AD campaign  that Tyran you needed millions of  dollars so he either had this money  himself or he had access to investors  who had this money b